{# Static locator map.

   An include, not a macro, because it reads `summit` from the page context —
   Nunjucks macros imported with `from` do not receive it.

   Deliberately NOT an embedded map. A Google Maps iframe sets third-party
   cookies on load, before consent; the site currently sets none, which is the
   only reason it carries no consent banner. This is a self-hosted raster from
   scripts/make-map.js wrapped in an outbound directions link, which does the
   same job for the visitor at no privacy cost. See docs/V3-SCOPE.md.

   Optional `locatorNote` sets the left-hand caption. #}
<figure class="locator">
  <a class="locator__frame"
     href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&amp;destination={{ summit.location.mapQuery | urlencode }}"
     target="_blank" rel="noopener">
    <picture>
      <source srcset="/img/map-kicc.avif" type="image/avif">
      <img src="/img/map-kicc.webp" width="768" height="512"
           loading="lazy" decoding="async"
           alt="Street map of central Nairobi. The Kenyatta International Convention Centre is marked on Harambee Avenue, between Parliament Road and Taifa Road, with Uhuru Park to the west.">
    </picture>
  </a>
  <figcaption class="locator__meta">
    <p>{{ locatorNote or "Opens Google Maps directions in a new tab." }}</p>
    <p>Map data &copy; <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenStreetMap</a> contributors</p>
  </figcaption>
</figure>
